[gd_scene format=3]

; The Crucible, under the Quench and the Basalt (map offset (191.5, -214.5)): where the machines' plating was cast. A great
; crucible hangs tilted over the casting floor, pouring into molds that still glow (jumped, or walked through once plated).
; Heat plating lies on a dais between them, and a shrine. West, the coolant falls from the Quench's drain into a basin, and
; gantries climb back up to it (the way out, needing nothing); east, the hole from the Basalt drops onto the floor.

